   2026-08-24 instead: Claude accepts 32 MB and 600 PAGES on 1M-context models — the 100-page figure
   is the 200k-context one — and Gemini accepts 50 MB / 1000 pages at a flat 258 tokens per page. The
   format was never the constraint; the binding cost is TOKENS (~800 per full-view page). So the
   budget became a spend decision derived from the take's own length: 2.5 frames per second, floor
   96, ceiling 300 (≈236k tokens, ≈11 MB), with a hard stop at 28 MB so a pathological recording
   degrades by stopping rather than by being rejected. On PO's take the budget stopped binding at
   all — the content earned 165 frames of an allowed 243. LESSON, and it is note 10's shape again:
   the instrument was a REMEMBERED NUMBER. Verify a platform limit before designing around it.
